---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import LiveTimes from "../components/LiveTimes.astro";
import { SITE, SOURCES } from "../lib/site";

import widgets from "../assets/widgets.jpeg";
import widgetsDark from "../assets/widgets-dark.jpeg";
import main from "../assets/screen-main-1.jpeg";
import mainDark from "../assets/screen-main-dark-1.jpeg";
import qibla from "../assets/screen-qibla.jpeg";

const shots = [
  {
    src: main,
    alt: "The app showing today's seven prayer times for Gombak, Selangor",
  },
  {
    src: widgets,
    alt: "Four simplesolat widget styles on an Android home screen",
  },
  { src: mainDark, alt: "The app in dark mode" },
  { src: widgetsDark, alt: "The widgets in dark mode" },
  { src: qibla, alt: "The Qibla compass" },
];
---

<Base>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>simplesolat</h1>
    <p class="tagline">{SITE.tagline}</p>
    <p>
      A free prayer times app for Android. Home screen widgets that follow you
      when you travel, reminders for every prayer, and all seven times,
      including Syuruk. No ads, no account, and your location never leaves your
      phone.
    </p>
    <p class="actions">
      <a class="button" href={SITE.playStore}>
        Get it on Google Play
      </a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="#times">
        See today's times
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <div id="times">
    <LiveTimes />
  </div>

  <h2 id="features">What it does</h2>
  <ul class="features">
    <li>
      <strong>Widgets that update themselves.</strong> Several styles, light and
      dark. They refresh in the background, and when you travel into a new zone,
      they switch to it on their own. No opening the app at the start of each
      month.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>All seven times.</strong> Imsak, Fajr, Syuruk, Dhuhr, Asr, Maghrib
      and Isha, with the current one highlighted. Syuruk tells you when the time
      for Fajr ends.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Reminders</strong> when each prayer time begins.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A Qibla compass.</strong>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Works offline.</strong> Timetables are kept on your phone for
      weeks ahead.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Works in many countries.</strong> Official timetables for nine
      countries, and calculated times everywhere else.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Free, with no ads and no account.</strong> The code is
      <a href={SITE.github}>public on GitHub</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="shots" role="list">
    {shots.map((s) => (
      <div role="listitem">
        <Image src={s.src} alt={s.alt} widths={[240, 480]} sizes="240px" />
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2 id="sources">Where the times come from</h2>
  <p>
    Wherever there's an official timetable, simplesolat uses it, taken from each
    country's religious authority:
  </p>
  <table class="sources">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Country</th>
        <th>Official source</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {SOURCES.map((s) => (
        <tr>
          <td>{s.country}</td>
          <td>
            <a href={s.url}>{s.authority}</a>
          </td>
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Everywhere else, the app calculates the times on your phone, using the
    method that's usual in your country, and the prayer times above do the same
    in your browser. Zone boundaries come from
    <a href="https://www.geoboundaries.org/">geoBoundaries</a>, and country
    borders from <a href="https://www.naturalearthdata.com/">Natural Earth</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    simplesolat works out your prayer zone <strong>on your phone</strong>, by
    checking your location against zone boundaries it has downloaded. Your
    location is never sent anywhere. The only thing the app asks a server for is
    the timetable for your zone.
  </p>
  <p>
    There's no account, no analytics and no ads. Read the
    <a href="/privacy/">full privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="help">Help</h2>

  <h3>Reminders arrive late, or not at all</h3>
  <p>
    Many Android phones stop apps running in the background to save battery,
    which delays reminders and widget updates. Set simplesolat's battery usage
    to <em>Unrestricted</em> (usually under Settings › Apps › simplesolat ›
    Battery), and allow <em>Alarms &amp; reminders</em> if your phone asks. The
    exact steps differ by brand;
    <a href="https://dontkillmyapp.com/">Don't kill my app!</a> has a guide for
    each one.
  </p>

  <h3>The widget isn't updating</h3>
  <p>
    It's usually the same battery setting as above. Widgets refresh in the
    background about every 15 minutes, and when a prayer time begins.
  </p>

  <h3>It shows the wrong zone</h3>
  <p>
    Check that location is turned on and allowed for simplesolat. The zone is
    worked out from your location, so a rough or old location can land you in a
    neighbouring zone.
  </p>

  <h3>The times are slightly different from my mosque</h3>
  <p>
    Where there's an official timetable, the app uses it exactly. Local mosques
    sometimes adjust by a minute or two. Outside those nine countries, times are
    calculated, and can differ a little from local practice.
  </p>

  <p>
    Something else? <a href={SITE.issues}>Open an issue on GitHub</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="developers">For developers</h2>
  <p>
    The prayer times behind simplesolat are public: static files on a CDN, with
    zones, boundaries and monthly timetables, readable from any website. This
    page reads them straight from your browser. See
    <a href={SITE.data}>simplesolat-data</a> for the format and the sources.
  </p>

  <h2 id="story">Why it exists</h2>
  <p>
    simplesolat started after the free prayer app I relied on stopped working,
    and I found out why.
    <a href={SITE.story}>Read the story</a>.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .tagline {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .features {
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }
  .features li + li {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
  .shots {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    padding-block: 1.5rem 0.5rem;
    scroll-snap-type: x mandatory;
  }
  .shots > div {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    scroll-snap-align: start;
  }
  .shots :global(img) {
    width: 240px;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 14px;
  }
  .sources {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .sources th,
  .sources td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
</style>
